---
// LocalStack · Lesson 3 — Lambda in Python: role, zip, deploy, invoke, logs.
import Lesson from "../../../../layouts/Lesson.astro";
const titlePt = "LocalStack 3 — Lambda em Python";
const titleEn = "LocalStack 3 — Lambda in Python";
const titleFallback = "LocalStack 3 — Lambda em Python";
const bodyClass = "lang-pt";
const viewport = "width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0";
const assets = [
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/style.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/dark.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/i18n.css\" />",
	"<script src=\"../assets/i18n.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/nav.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/reading-ui.js\" defer></script>",
];
---
<Lesson
	titlePt={titlePt}
	titleEn={titleEn}
	titleFallback={titleFallback}
	bodyClass={bodyClass}
	viewport={viewport}
	assets={assets}
>
	<Fragment is:raw>
    <article class="lesson">
      <header class="hero">
        <span class="eyebrow">⬡ LocalStack · Lição 3 · Médio</span>
        <h1>
          <span data-lang="pt">Lambda em Python: do zip ao log</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Lambda in Python: from zip to log</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lead">
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >O ciclo completo de uma função: <strong>role → zip → deploy →
            invoke → logs</strong>. Depois desta lição, você nunca mais copia
            um tutorial de Lambda às cegas.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >The full function cycle: <strong>role → zip → deploy → invoke →
            logs</strong>. After this lesson you never copy a Lambda tutorial
            blind again.</span
          >
        </p>
      </header>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">1</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">O modelo: handler, evento e runtime</span
        ><span data-lang="en">The model: handler, event and runtime</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Lambda roda <strong>uma função sua em resposta a um evento</strong>.
          O runtime (Python, Node…) injeta um <code>dict</code>/<code>objeto</code>
          descrevendo o que aconteceu, e lê o que você retorna. Nada de
          servidor — <strong>you função é a unidade de deploy</strong>.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Lambda runs <strong>your function in response to an event</strong>.
          The runtime (Python, Node…) injects a <code>dict</code>/<code>object</code>
          describing what happened, and reads what you return. No server —
          <strong>the function is the deploy unit</strong>.</span
        >
      </p>
      <pre class="block"><code><span class="c"># lambda_function.py — o menor handler útil</span>
<span class="k">import</span> json

<span class="k">def</span> <span class="k">handler</span>(event, context):
    name = event.get(<span class="s">"name"</span>, <span class="s">"mundo"</span>)
    print(<span class="s">f"recebi: </span>{json.dumps(event)}<span class="s">"</span>)  <span class="c"># vira log</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> {
        <span class="s">"statusCode"</span>: 200,
        <span class="s">"body"</span>: json.dumps({<span class="s">"msg"</span>: <span class="s">f"ola, </span>{name}<span class="s">"</span>}),
    }</code></pre>
      <div class="callout key">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          ><code>print</code> em Python vira <strong>linha de log no
          CloudWatch</strong> — é o seu <code>console.log</code> de produção.
          Sem ele, você depura no escuro.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Python <code>print</code> becomes a <strong>CloudWatch log
          line</strong> — it is your production <code>console.log</code>.
          Without it you debug in the dark.</span
        >
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">2</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Deploy em 4 comandos</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Deploy in 4 commands</span>
      </h2>
      <pre class="block"><code><span class="c"># 1 — a role de execução (quem a função "é" ao rodar)</span>
awslocal iam create-role \
  --role-name lambda-python-role \
  --assume-role-policy-document <span class="s">'{"Version":"2012-10-17",
    "Statement":[{"Effect":"Allow","Principal":{"Service":"lambda.amazonaws.com"},
    "Action":"sts:AssumeRole"}]}'</span>

<span class="c"># 2 — empacote</span>
zip -j function.zip lambda_function.py

<span class="c"># 3 — crie a função</span>
awslocal lambda create-function \
  --function-name ola-python \
  --runtime python3.12 \
  --handler lambda_function.handler \
  --zipfile fileb://function.zip \
  --role arn:aws:iam::000000000000:role/lambda-python-role

<span class="c"># 4 — invoque</span>
awslocal lambda invoke \
  --payload <span class="s">'{"name":"Patricio"}'</span> \
  --cli-binary-format raw-in-base64-out \
  out.json &amp;&amp; cat out.json</code></pre>
      <pre class="block"><code>cat out.json
<span class="c"># esperado / expected:</span>
<span class="s">{"statusCode": 200, "body": "{\"msg\": \"ola, Patricio\"}"}</span></code></pre>
      <div class="callout warn">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Sem <code>--cli-binary-format raw-in-base64-out</code>, o CLI v3
          exige payload em base64 e o invoke falha com mensagem críptica.
          <strong>Coloque no seu vocabulário permanente.</strong></span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Without <code>--cli-binary-format raw-in-base64-out</code>, CLI v2+
          expects a base64 payload and the invoke fails cryptically.
          <strong>Add it to your permanent vocabulary.</strong></span
        >
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">3</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Logs: o feedback loop da função</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Logs: the function's feedback loop</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Cada função ganha um <strong>log group
          <code>/aws/lambda/&lt;nome&gt;</code></strong>. O tail é o seu melhor
          amigo durante o desafio.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Each function gets a <strong>log group
          <code>/aws/lambda/&lt;name&gt;</code></strong>. The tail is your best
          friend during the challenge.</span
        >
      </p>
      <pre class="block"><code><span class="c"># os últimos eventos de log da função</span>
awslocal logs tail /aws/lambda/ola-python --since 5m

<span class="c"># esperado (entre outras linhas) / expected:</span>
<span class="s">recebi: {"name": "Patricio"}</span></code></pre>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">4</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Desafio (médio): contador em env var</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Challenge (medium): counter in an env var</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="callout key">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          ><strong>Objetivo:</strong> uma função Python que lê a variável de
          ambiente <code>PLACE</code> e devolve
          <code>{"msg": "ola de &lt;PLACE&gt;"}</code>. Você não pode recriar a
          função — <strong>atualize-a</strong>.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          ><strong>Goal:</strong> a Python function that reads the
          <code>PLACE</code> environment variable and returns
          <code>{"msg": "ola from &lt;PLACE&gt;"}</code>. You cannot recreate
          the function — <strong>update it</strong>.</span
        >
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>
          <span data-lang="pt">Passos</span><span data-lang="en">Steps</span>
        </h3>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt">Edite o handler para ler
            <code>os.environ["PLACE"]</code>.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Edit the handler to read
            <code>os.environ["PLACE"]</code>.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt">Re-zipe e atualize o código:</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Re-zip and update the code:</span>
            <code>awslocal lambda update-function-code --function-name ola-python --zipfile fileb://function.zip</code>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt">Defina a config (env vars):</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Set the config (env vars):</span>
            <code>awslocal lambda update-function-configuration --function-name ola-python --environment "Variables={PLACE=localstack}"</code>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <pre class="block"><code>awslocal lambda invoke --payload <span class="s">'{}'</span> \
  --cli-binary-format raw-in-base64-out out.json &amp;&amp; cat out.json
<span class="c"># esperado / expected:</span>
<span class="s">{"statusCode": 200, "body": "{\"msg\": \"ola de localstack\"}"}</span></code></pre>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">5</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Recupere sem pistas</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Retrieve without clues</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">Qual o log group de uma Lambda?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">What is a Lambda's log group?</span>
          </summary>
          <p><code>/aws/lambda/&lt;nome-da-funcao&gt;</code></p>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">Atualizar código vs configuração — quais comandos?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Update code vs config — which commands?</span>
          </summary>
          <p><code>update-function-code</code> · <code>update-function-configuration</code></p>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">O que a role de execução representa?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">What does the execution role represent?</span>
          </summary>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt">As permissões da função ao rodar (quem ela
            "é").</span
            ><span data-lang="en">The function's permissions at runtime (who
            it "is").</span>
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">Como ver logs de 5 minutos atrás?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">How to see the last 5 minutes of logs?</span>
          </summary>
          <p><code>awslocal logs tail /aws/lambda/f --since 5m</code></p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <footer class="lesson-foot">
        <div>
          <span data-lang="pt">Fonte primária:</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Primary source:</span>
          <a href="https://docs.localstack.cloud/aws/services/lambda/"
            >LocalStack · Lambda</a
          >
        </div>
        <a class="next-card" href="0004-lambda-typescript.html"
          ><span class="lbl"
            ><span data-lang="pt">Próxima lição</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Next lesson</span></span
          >
          <div class="t">
            <span data-lang="pt">Lambda em TypeScript — o mesmo pelo Node →</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Lambda in TypeScript — same, via Node →</span>
          </div></a
        >
        <div>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Algo não ficou claro? Pergunte ao agente — ele é seu
            professor.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >Anything unclear? Ask the agent—your teacher.</span
          >
          · <a href="../../../index.html">⬡ Hub</a>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </article>
  </Fragment>
</Lesson>
